#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/id #uuid "dd9a05fb-f01c-5ec2-a984-9d73584065ef" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9683" :question/problem "Which of the lines $p,q,r$, or $s$ is the trend line of the scatter plot above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/65c7bafdfde0ba8015d87c0888f1bdcd.png)" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a curve, not a straight line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/0e32e7767c5353f75f4d693d454192a4.png)\n\nTherefore, there is no linear trend in the data."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/id #uuid "245065cc-c95c-5f93-bf7d-bbb6412a27e9" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9694" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the trend line shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/9bb0151238440704095e29f3bd632b5f.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points\n\n$$\n(x_1,y_1)=(-4,5)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(x_2,y_2)=(5,-4)\n$$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= (-4 - 5)/(5 - (-4)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-9}{9} \\\\\n&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-1$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny =-x + b\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b$. We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(5,-4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= -x + b \\\\\n- 4 &= -5 + b \\\\\n1 &= b \\\\\nb &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is\n\n$$\ny =-x + 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/id #uuid "1a299957-af22-544b-af37-695f45065a3e" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9695" :question/problem "Estimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/ebdab620e3e2f624fd9b67cec07fee36.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/f09eeb54cefd8a6e6c7de8a1508acae8.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through\n\n$$\n(x_1,y_1)\\approx(4,4)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(x_2,y_2)\\approx(6,7)\n$$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\nm \\mid \\approx \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}}; = \\frac{7 - 4}{6 - 4}; = \\frac{3}{2}; = 1.5\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=1.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny = 1.5 x + b\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b$. We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(4,4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= 1.5x + b \\\\\n4 &= 1.5(4) + b \\\\\n4 &= 6 + b \\\\\n- 2 &= b \\\\\nb &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is\n\n$$\ny = 1.5x - 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c199cc-b457-5100-a811-b770c11dec04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no linear trend in the data" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148963} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a21e45-42d1-5f04-b97d-424d712eb134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148964} {:answer/id #uuid "29ce39ad-de7a-5ea5-b4fa-368cb0ca5dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148965} {:answer/id #uuid "323d8b11-4d41-5c2f-b1b5-395f84634905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148966} {:answer/id #uuid "735fa2fc-9d4a-5845-b0d1-332279944de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "323d8b11-4d41-5c2f-b1b5-395f84634905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148966} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5cddbed-708c-5216-ada4-a2e6b63a2ba6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148962}] :question/id #uuid "fa90d9a6-e51c-5604-b79f-b37b09fca968" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133633" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/q-133633.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between age and years of work experience among a particular group of workers. Which of the following could be the trend line for this scatter plot?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81fcd057-f612-59c5-9b08-3ba76a86c466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148981} {:answer/id #uuid "